y as her on her  the first pretty much full day of her  job to talk about climate change and  analyna bearbox throughout all her  meetings today has made it extremely  clear that obviously while she's foreign  minister as a green elected politician  part of her foreign policy is going to  be about dealing with the climate crisis  and there's no question that john  kerry's place as the special envoy from  the white house on this issue  that that is an important meeting for  her to have had and she also had  meetings today with the head of nato and  with the european union's foreign policy  chief what does this tell us about the  imprint that she hopes to make on the  european stage  well it's really interesting that she  came here and she had all of these very  senior meetings and specifically on  security and defense policy as well  which is obviously a big part of her job  as the foreign minister of germany i  think in the post-medical era these  questions surrounding  you know who would take over who would  uh continue  this sort of line of miracles government  and one thing that annalina bearbox has  been keen to do is to show continuity  she's obviously from a different party  that not everybody  here in brussels knows her too well but  she tried to say listen on the issues of  the of belarus and the stuff that's  going on at the border there we  still want to put pressure on the  government in minsk the troop built up  on ukraine's border by russia she  continued to say that to condemn that  and to say uh that nato and the european  union need to act together on those  issues and so i think she was there to  also show some continuity from the  previous government even though the  issues that all the sides and all the  sides will eventually have to discuss  uh it's quite new for her on her first  day  and we know jack what she's trying to  project but what about the people that  she was meeting today i mean do we know  how she was truly received  i think she was